WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:00.550 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  ncis has stood head and shoulders above  most of its police procedural peers for  years thanks to its lovable cast of  eclectic characters and almost uncanny  longevity the cbs show has been running  since 2003 and the ongoing season 19  finds the series as strong as usual  however it's clear that the show's  arguably most massive change yet is on  the not too distant horizon and it's  been looking that way for a while for 18  years the stalwart leader of the titular  investigation team in ncis has been led  by leroy jethro gibbs played by mark  harmon who was the backbone of the show  throughout its first 18 seasons season  19 of ncis has revealed that new  developments along with 18 seasons of  hard-hitting investigations weighing  down on his broad shoulders have caused  gibbs to decide that he's done with his  ncis job and that he's planning to carve  a new life for himself in alaska it's an  understandable development for the  character for anyone who watched the  season 18 finale the episode showed  gibbs boarding a boat that wasn't  destined to last long as it sailed out  to sea it unexpectedly blew up  fortunately fans saw gibb's body not  long afterward with him soon swimming to  shore it let everyone know gibbs would  return for season 19 but it definitely  gave the impression he wasn't going to  be around much longer but what exactly  caused the character to decide so or  rather what prompted mark harmon to join  the many actors who have left ncis the  hollywood reporter states mark harmon's  exit from the show is a pretty final one  at least in his starring capacity after  all the star is only signed for a  limited amount of episodes for season 19  and gives gibbs decision to remain in  alaska pretty much removes him from the  fabric of the show for the foreseeable  future what's more the ongoing season  features some brand new star power in  the form of katrina law and rumored  harmon replacement gary cole harmon's  limited episode deal means that gibbs  has effectively left his active role in  the show behind but showrunner stephen d  binder is quick to note that the actor  will maintain a behind the scenes role  and there's always a chance for an  on-screen comeback as well binder stated  as an executive producer and dear friend  mark continues to be an integral part of  the fabric of the show our north star  has always been staying true to our  characters and that truth has always  guided the stories we tell and where  those characters go so regarding the  future of gibbs as longtime fans of the  show may have noticed over the years  never count leroy jethro gives out that  means viewers may not have shed their  last tears over gibbs just yet if we  were into betting we'd be willing to put  down money on mark harmon returning for  the series finale whenever that occurs  it's hard to say goodbye to a beloved tv  character especially one who's been on  the air for nearly two decades leroy  jethro gibb starred in hundreds of ncis  episodes and has earned a special place  in people's hearts the show just won't  be the same without him and fans have  already taken to social media to let  their thoughts known on the emotional  departure it's entirely possible his  final scene of fishing on a lake and the  great unknown will be the last time  audiences see gibbs but at least he  received the send-off he so richly  deserved fans were quick to chime in  with their thoughts one fan wrote i am  sad gibbs is leaving ncis i got to  respect and applaud mark harmon for his  performance through 18 years as gibbs  another fan noted i just learned mark  harmon is leaving ncis and i'm in  complete shock i grew up with ncis and  especially with agent leroy jethro gibbs  but he did his time and i'm really proud  he had such an amazing journey gibbs has  certainly come a long way ever since he  first graced people's screens on the  episode ice queen on jag he'd only  appear on one more jag episode before  spinning off into ncis where he's been  ever since harmon walked away when the  time was right just like the great gibbs  so famously said when the job is done  walk away  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite tv shows and movies are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  you

